(LST-49 — a missing key does not crash: the lookup sets the error flag,
 so an `on error` handler reacts. RULE CHANGED, 2026-08-22 (0.4.10,
 #72/#91): the PROVABLE case (a literal map, first block below) still
 yields the number 0, unchanged from 0.4.9. The UNPROVABLE case (a
 `Set`-grown map, second block) is new territory — pre-0.4.10 it also
 yielded a raw untyped 0, which a text/list/map destination would
 dereference as a pointer and segfault (#91); now it yields the
 destination's own typed default (empty text / [] / {}) instead.
 Also covers: LST-51 (the worked example of LANGUAGE.md:2560-2561).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST-49.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   0
   missing
   2
   0
   1
   0
   0
)
a map called person is {"name": "Ada", "age": 36}.
print person's "nope".
on error print "missing".
print person's length.

a map called grown is {}.
set grown's "k1" to "v1".
a text called misstext is grown's "nope2".
a buffer called misscheck is misstext.
print misscheck's size.
print misscheck's empty.
a list called misslist is grown's "nope3".
print misslist's length.
a map called missmap is grown's "nope4".
print missmap's length.
